# house-pause-save-commit-empty — the EMPTY-slot commit path ("create a new save"):
# open the PAUSE Save submenu, DOWN once onto the unoccupied slot 1, then A → the
# slot is empty (playtime==0) so FUN_0047f5bc commits AT ONCE (no "Overwriting
# file." dialog) — the 60-frame commit animation runs and the was-NO-DATA card
# fills in with the live game's stats.  The companion of house-pause-save-commit
# (which takes the OCCUPIED slot-0 overwrite path); together they cover both
# A-confirm branches of FUN_0047f5bc.
#
# Derived from house-pause-save-nav / -commit (identical open path: load fa7c82 →
# HOUSE free-roam idle, {phasepin 80}; ESC → 3×down → Z opens Save;
# SAVE_PICKER_READY rebases the picker-time inputs past the per-side pause ramp).
#
# Commit drive (relative to SAVE_PICKER_READY):
#   DOWN @20 : cursor 0→1 (within the 5-row window, no slide) — slot 1 = NO-DATA.
#   A    @40 : slot 1 is empty (playtime 0) ⇒ FUN_0047f5bc sets DAT_074b289c=1
#              directly (no dialog), the commit sequence runs (snapshot + the save
#              jingle + FUN_004905a8(1) working→slot 1 copy/checksum/write) and
#              c89c counts 1→0x3c (60f) driving the progress bar + card pulse on
#              the now-occupied slot-1 card.
#   idle     : c89c wraps, the picker rests showing the newly-saved slot 1.
# The SAVE virtualization ({savefile}) sandboxes the write.
# embedded save: fa7c820333914d2a045f1003dc78c4b65fb04235e8d37f032c0f1e0aeb761c54
